# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Postgres
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these from your Supabase project:
#   Top of dashboard → Connect → ORMs → Prisma tab
# Substitute [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the DB password you set when creating
# the project.

# Pooled connection (port 6543) — used at runtime by PrismaClient
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-1-ap-northeast-2.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"

# Direct connection (port 5432) — used only by `prisma migrate`
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.YOUR_PROJECT_REF:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-1-ap-northeast-2.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase API + Storage
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these from: Project Settings → API
# The first two are browser-safe (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix exposes them to client).
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is server-only — never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_,
# never import it from a client component.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...."
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...."

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One-time setup checklist (not env vars — just a reminder)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create the Supabase project in Seoul (ap-northeast-2) for low latency
# 2. Storage → New bucket → name: site-photos → toggle "Public bucket"
# 3. Run: npx prisma migrate dev
# 4. After changing your Supabase project ref, update the hostname in
#    next.config.ts (images.remotePatterns)
